<urn:atm:triage:finding/AX5-QA3-004>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AX5-QA3-004" ;
  triage:title "emit_task_reminder's generic Herdr emission-failure branch records no stats counter and does not stamp the per-member cooldown guard" ;
  triage:description "AX.5 QA-3 (quality-mgr ax5-qa-r3, PR #1201 Final Quality Report 2026-09-05T15:09Z) at head c4b8e3f2acdc4e7b5e88f37a335df4c73255fdea; req-qa finding confirmed real by quality-mgr direct code read. In emit_task_reminder (crates/atm-http-runtime/src/herdr_queue_wake.rs:535-538) the match on emit_received_message has three arms: Ok -> record_task_outcome (counts and stamps), Err(HerdrUnavailable) -> stats.breaker_open += 1, and a generic Err(error) arm that only logs a structured warn!. The generic failure arm neither increments any HerdrQueueWakeStats counter nor calls stamp_task_attempt, so a member whose reminder emission fails for a non-breaker reason is retried on every tick with no cooldown and the failure is invisible to the stats surface used by the Property 5/6 assertions. Fix: add a dedicated failure counter (e.g. task_reminders_failed) and stamp the cooldown guard in that arm, mirroring the sibling arms; add a clock-seam test where the emitter returns a non-HerdrUnavailable error and assert the counter and the cooldown." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ax" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "REQ-QA" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:closedAt "2026-09-05T15:36:45Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedBy "quality-mgr" ;
  triage:closureNote "Closure confirmed by quality-mgr follow-up QA; Resolution event triage:r59 in .sprints/AX/events.ttl; final sprint verdict AX5-QA4 PASS (PR #1201 comment 5552870450)." ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-05T15:09:40Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
